title: mf repo borrow
tags: [[CLI command]] Sync
kind: reference
summary: Borrow a repository of another machine, through a mount of its files

Copies the `.metafolder/` of a repository mounted from another machine to `--to`, a new
local directory, marks the remote borrowed, and loads the copy — under `--name` when the
remote's name is already loaded here. Refused while the remote's own daemon has it
loaded, unless `--force` overrides a holder file a crash left. `mf repo give-back` sends
it home ([[Cross-machine sync]]).
